I think the issue we&#39;re having with RStan crashing is<br>due to not catching exceptions everywhere we need to.<br>The good news is that it should be easy to fix before<br>the next release.<br><br><br>This model:<br><br>mod1.stan<br>-------------------------------------------<br>parameters {<br>   real y;<br>}<br>transformed parameters {<br>   matrix[3,3] z;<br>   real z44;<br>   z44 &lt;- sqrt(z[4,4]);<br>}<br>model {<br>   y ~ normal(0,1);<br>}<br>-------------------------------------------<br><br><br>causes the following behavior in RStan 1.2.0 (on the<br>R 2.15.3 GUI):<br><br><br>============================================================<br> &gt; stan(&#39;mod1.stan&#39;)<br><br>TRANSLATING MODEL &#39;mod1&#39; FROM Stan CODE TO C++ CODE NOW.<br>COMPILING THE C++ CODE FOR MODEL &#39;mod1&#39; NOW.<br>SAMPLING FOR MODEL &#39;mod1&#39; NOW (CHAIN 1).<br>Iteration:    1 / 2000 [  0%]  (Adapting)<br><br>  *** caught segfault ***<br>address 0x1636d647b, cause &#39;memory not mapped&#39;<br><br>Traceback:<br>  1: .External(list(name = &quot;CppMethod__invoke_notvoid&quot;, address = &lt;pointer: 0x1023c9920&gt;,     dll = list(name = &quot;Rcpp&quot;, <br>path = &quot;/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/2.15/Resources/library/Rcpp/libs/x86_64/Rcpp.so&quot;,         dynamicLookup <br>= TRUE, handle = &lt;pointer: 0x10c513e90&gt;,         info = &lt;pointer: 0x10041bd78&gt;), numParameters = -1L),     &lt;pointer: <br>0x10131ab90&gt;, &lt;pointer: 0x1013ce440&gt;, .pointer,     ...)<br>  2: sampler$call_sampler(args_list[[i]])<br>  3: doTryCatch(return(expr), name, parentenv, handler)<br>  4: tryCatchOne(expr, names, parentenv, handlers[[1L]])<br>  5: tryCatchList(expr, classes, parentenv, handlers)<br>  6: tryCatch(expr, error = function(e) {    call &lt;- conditionCall(e)    if (!is.null(call)) {        if <br>(identical(call[[1L]], quote(doTryCatch)))             call &lt;- sys.call(-4L)        dcall &lt;- deparse(call)[1L] <br>prefix &lt;- paste(&quot;Error in&quot;, dcall, &quot;: &quot;)        LONG &lt;- 75L        msg &lt;- conditionMessage(e)        sm &lt;- strsplit(msg, <br>&quot;
&quot;)[[1L]]        w &lt;- 14L + nchar(dcall, type = &quot;w&quot;) + nchar(sm[1L], type = &quot;w&quot;)        if (<a href="http://is.na" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792476814511000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1otOW1GrsfwA8JHiPOgq1D">is.na</a>(w))             w &lt;- <br>14L + nchar(dcall, type = &quot;b&quot;) + nchar(sm[1L],                 type = &quot;b&quot;)        if (w &gt; LONG)             prefix &lt;- <br>paste0(prefix, &quot;
  &quot;)    }    else prefix &lt;- &quot;Error : &quot;    msg &lt;- paste0(prefix, conditionMessage(e), &quot;
&quot;) <br>.Internal(seterrmessage(msg[1L]))    if (!silent &amp;&amp; identical(getOption(&quot;show.error.messages&quot;),         TRUE)) { <br>cat(msg, file = stderr())        .Internal(printDeferredWarnings())    }    invisible(structure(msg, class = <br>&quot;try-error&quot;, condition = e))})<br>  7: try(sampler$call_sampler(args_list[[i]]))<br>  8: .local(object, ...)<br>  9: sampling(sm, data, pars, chains, iter, warmup, thin, seed, init,     sample_file = sample_file, verbose = verbose, <br>check_data = TRUE,     ...)<br>10: sampling(sm, data, pars, chains, iter, warmup, thin, seed, init,     sample_file = sample_file, verbose = verbose, <br>check_data = TRUE,     ...)<br>11: stan(&quot;mod1.stan&quot;)<br><br>Possible actions:<br>1: abort (with core dump, if enabled)<br>2: normal R exit<br>3: exit R without saving workspace<br>4: exit R saving workspace<br>Selection:<br>======================================<br><br><br><br>What I don&#39;t understand is that the same model from<br>the command line does this (this is from an up to date<br>git pull on the command line in Mac OS X):<br><br>=========================================================<br>~/stan(master)$ make CC=clang++ O=0 ../temp2/crash/mod1<br><br>--- Translating Stan graphical model to C++ code ---<br>bin/stanc ../temp2/crash/mod1.stan --o=../temp2/crash/mod1.cpp<br>Model name=mod1_model<br>Input file=../temp2/crash/mod1.stan<br>Output file=../temp2/crash/mod1.cpp<br>clang++ -I src -I lib/eigen_3.1.2 -I lib/boost_1.53.0 -Wall -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE <br>-DBOOST_DISABLE_ASSERTS -Wno-unused-function -Wno-tautological-compare   -c -O0 -o ../temp2/crash/mod1.o <br>../temp2/crash/mod1.cpp<br>clang++ -I src -I lib/eigen_3.1.2 -I lib/boost_1.53.0 -Wall -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE <br>-DBOOST_DISABLE_ASSERTS -Wno-unused-function -Wno-tautological-compare    -O0 -o ../temp2/crash/mod1 <br>../temp2/crash/mod1.o -Lbin -lstan<br>~/stan(master)$<br>~/stan(master)$ ../temp2/crash/mod1<br><br>Exception: INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=4; lower bound=1; upper bound=3; index position=1; z<br><br>Diagnostic information:<br>Dynamic exception type: std::out_of_range<br>std::exception::what: INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=4; lower bound=1; upper bound=3; index position=1; z<br><br><br>~/stan(master)$<br>=========================================================<br><br><br>- Bob<br>
